{
  "case_id": "2019-18-776",
  "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "PAUL W. HUGHES, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners.\nFREDERICK LIU, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section (2)(D) provides for review of questions of law decided by the Board of Immigration Appeals. I'll start with where we and the government agree. At minimum, courts may review whether the Board identified the proper legal standard. The government agrees."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, before you get to that, I wonder if you have not read too much into the government's statement that a -- that under their theory, it would be permissible for a court to review not just whether the -- the -- the Board articulated the right theory but whether it actually used the right theory."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What does that teach us about the -- the question before us?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Hughes, I mean, I think the question that Justice Gorsuch asked is a very broad one, and it's -- it's with respect not just to the diligence but to all these other Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: On the statutory history point that Justice Kagan raised, St. Cyr involves what the Court characterized as pure questions of law. Congress, we know, then comes in, and there are a variety of statutes, as you're aware, that refer to mixed questions, but Congress in this statute does not refer specifically to mixed questions. So, if you put those two things together, you would lean toward reading this statute to refer to what one might call pure questions of law. That's the government's argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Can you succinctly tell me what the questions of law are in your two cases?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Is it the government's position that only pure questions of law are reviewable, or is it also the government's position that there can be some applications that are so egregious that they would rise to the level of being questions of law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: The text says questions of law. And I can find statutes that use those words, and they clearly mean both, as they say."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Liu",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LIU: -- I -- I think it's fair to look at the context in which Congress looked -- wrote this statute. As I said at the outset, I think the context here points in a very clear direction. I mean, this was a Congress whose primary policy preference was to give criminal aliens no judicial review at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Liu",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LIU: And I think they would have wanted that because their goal all along, since 1996, is to -- is to expedite the removal of criminal aliens."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Liu, there is no question that we have a presumption in favor of judicial review, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: It begs -- it begs the question, doesn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Have you finished?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, I take that point. I mean, that's why I asked about what's the nature of this presumption, because, if this presumption is only about congressional intent, it has to fight against a pretty strong sense that Congress wanted to do something significant here about cutting off review for criminal aliens."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But suppose that you take that presumption, very interesting and deep question that I have, and maybe you have a view on this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-776",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: And what do you think?"
    },
    {
